    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into August 13th with a strategic emphasis on capitalizing against Andrew Abbott\u2019s high-xERA profile. **Miguel Vargas** leads our output today with a score of 63.96, benefiting from a prime #3 spot and a favorable matchup against the left-handed Abbott. While **Kyle Tucker** (60.91) remains a cornerstone, his production is slightly tempered by a matchup against Shane Drohan; however, his elite profile keeps him firmly in the \"Strong\" start tier. We are also leaning on **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (58.31) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (58.18) to provide stability in the middle of our lineup; both players benefit from dynamic platoon factors that counteract the moderate skill levels of their respective opposing starters, allowing us to maintain a consistent scoring floor despite the absence of elite speed in these specific slots.\n\nOur most difficult decision of the morning centered on **Wade Meckler**, who sat just below our optimal cutoff with a score of 38.70. While his high-leverage leadoff role and platoon advantage against Jacob deGrom were enticing, the brutal matchup against a pitcher of deGrom\u2019s caliber ultimately tanked his projection. We prioritized the higher cumulative point expectations of **Sam Antonacci** (50.38) and **Andy Pages** (55.50) to preserve our game caps. Risk management remains the priority today: **Andy Pages** and **Kyle Tucker** carry \"Lineup Pending\" designations, meaning their scores are predicated on assumed spots in the order. If final lineups shift them out of the top-four, we will be forced to reconsider their impact on our daily Roto targets, particularly in a season where our strategy remains hyper-focused on efficiency over volume.",
